  "design_notes": [
    "The table covers the first stage. For the upper stage the design says only \"1 or 2 engines\": the two upper options have no engine-out column, no reliability modifier and no integration days. The sentence under the table gives the 2-engine option its strength and drawback; the 1-engine upper option has none.",
    "Reliability modifier: \"−0.3%\" is stored as reliability add −0.003 on the stage, which is percentage points (open question 9 in data/README.md). \"+0\" is stored as an add of 0. The word \"complexity\" printed with −0.3% is the note of that modifier.",
    "Integration: \"+3 days\" is game.integ_days 3. \"Fast\" (1 engine) is a strength text with no integ_days.",
    "engine_out_capability maps the Engine-out capable? column: No no, \"Partial (if TWR allows)\" partial, \"Yes, usually\" usually, Yes yes. engine_out_bonus is none, standard (\"engine-out bonus\") or strong (\"strong engine-out bonus\"); the bonus has no number in the design.",
    "Every multi-engine option enables MG-12 Engine-Out Rebalance (\"if an engine fails in a cluster\") and carries its fact F08. F27 (N1) is the line under the table and is kept at category level.",
    "\"Heavier thrust structure\" (5 engines) has no mass: flag heavier_thrust_structure.",
    "No contracts list: the design restricts no engine count (Appendix A shows 3 and 9 first-stage engines offered in C1). No model path: an engine count is not a model of its own."
  ],
